			<div class="content" id="post-content-4288340">
									

<p>Totally agree! I'm a big fan of what I call 'exploratory' SCP articles and stories, and I've been making a list of the best ones, like this one, for my own benefit but also because I've been tinkering with the idea of offering to make up a list of such articles on the 'User-Curated Lists' page, if there's enough interest.</p>
<p>Some random examples: SCP-093 &quot;Red Sea Object&quot;, with the amazing journeys into the hellish world it provides access to; SCP-1689 &quot;Bag Of Holding Potatoes&quot;, and the thrilling adventures in potato world; and SCP-2935 &quot;O, Death&quot;.</p>
<p>I have about another 30 possible articles noted so far.</p>
<p>I know I'm necroposting here, but if anyone reading this has any suggestions or feedback, I'd love to hear it!</p>
<p>EDIT: Since posting this, I've found an awesome source of 'exploration' articles already compiled: choose Tales from the banner menu, then incident reports, then the explorations tab. There are currently 49 entries.</p>

